{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "a-delegation-that-declares-architectureimpact-is-refused-unt",
  "title": "A delegation that declares architectureImpact is refused until the record carries an ARCH- decision, whatever the class says",
  "requirement": "REQ-308: a delegation that declares architectureImpact does not start without the architect's decision (an ARCH- entry in the Analysis Record decisions[]); the flag decides, not the derived class, so an omitted changeClass or changeClass L1 with the flag is refused too; L0, L1 and L2 without the flag are unaffected.",
  "kind": "regression",
  "status": "verified",
  "source": "agent",
  "automated": true,
  "testPath": "plugins/orchestrator/test/architect-consult-gate.test.mjs",
  "runCommand": "node --test plugins/orchestrator/test/architect-consult-gate.test.mjs",
  "steps": [
    "Mount the orchestrator with a fake board and the analysis service whose gate answers \"L1\" for an omitted changeClass, as the real store does.",
    "delegate_task with changeClass L2, architectureImpact true and a record whose decisions[] has no ARCH- entry: refused, no task row, no child.",
    "delegate_task with architectureImpact true and no changeClass: refused with the same code.",
    "delegate_task with changeClass L1 and architectureImpact true: refused with the same code.",
    "delegate_task with the flag and a record carrying {id:\"ARCH-1\"}: one task row, one child.",
    "delegate_task for L0, L1 and L2 without the flag: still pass."
  ],
  "expected": "delegate_task returns {ok:false, code:\"architect_consult_required\"} bearing a message that names decisions[] and ARCH-, and writes no task row and starts no child - for changeClass L2 with the flag, for the flag with no changeClass (the record answers L1) and for changeClass L1 with the flag; the same flagged delegation passes once decisions[] carries an ARCH- entry; L0, L1 and L2 without the flag pass unchanged.",
  "tags": [
    "orchestrator",
    "delegate_task",
    "DEC-002",
    "architect",
    "gate",
    "architectureImpact"
  ],
